   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* --- Glide reflections: the orientation-reversing case --- */\n\n/* Split the translation part relative to the mirror direction u = (cos α, sin α) */\nglide_parts(α, b) := block([u, bpar, bperp],\n  u     : [cos(α), sin(α)],\n  bpar  : tsimp( (b . u) * u ),\n  bperp : tsimp( b - bpar ),\n  [bpar, bperp] )$\n\n/* Case A: b entirely perpendicular to the mirror — this is a pure reflection,\n   in a line shifted by bperp/2.  It has a whole line of fixed points. */\nprint(\"--- b ⊥ mirror: a pure reflection in a shifted line ---\")$\ngp : glide_parts(0, [0, 2])$\nprint(\"mirror along the x-axis, b = (0,2)\")$\nprint(\"b∥ = \", gp[1], \"   b⊥ = \", gp[2])$\nfA(x) := tsimp( Ref(0) . cvec(x) + cvec([0, 2]) )$\nprint(\"f(0,1) = \", transpose(fA([0,1])), \"  (fixed — on the line y = 1)\")$\nprint(\"f(5,1) = \", transpose(fA([5,1])), \"  (fixed — the whole line y = 1)\")$\n\n/* Case B: b has a component along the mirror — no fixed point exists */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"--- b ∦ mirror: a genuine glide reflection ---\")$\ngp2 : glide_parts(0, [3, 2])$\nprint(\"mirror along the x-axis, b = (3,2)\")$\nprint(\"b∥ = \", gp2[1], \"   b⊥ = \", gp2[2])$\nfB(x) := tsimp( Ref(0) . cvec(x) + cvec([3, 2]) )$\nsolB : solve([3 + xx = xx, 2 - yy = yy], [xx, yy])$\nprint(\"fixed-point equations f(x)=x have solution set: \", solB, \"  (empty)\")$\nprint(\"but f∘f = \", transpose(fB(args(transpose(fB([xx, yy])))[1])),\n      \"  — a pure translation by 2b∥\")$",
